eratorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$"] [17592186335809 "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}t(1-\\operatorname{cos}t)-{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t & =\\operatorname{cos}t-{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t-{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}t-({\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}t-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t=1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}t(1-\\operatorname{cos}t)-{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t=\\operatorname{cos}t-1.\n$$"] [17592186335810 "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}t(\\operatorname{sin}t-1)+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t & ={\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t-\\operatorname{sin}t+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t \\\\  & =({\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t)-\\operatorname{sin}t \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{sin}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we simplified the right-hand side using ${\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}t=1.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}t(\\operatorname{sin}t-1)+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}t=1-\\operatorname{sin}t.\n$$"] [17592186335811 "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\\theta {\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta +{\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\cdot ({\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta +{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta )\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta +{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\cdot ({\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}\\theta +{cos}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\\theta {\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}\\theta +{\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}\\theta .\n$$"] [17592186335815 "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}x{\\operatorname{cos}}^{3}x+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot ({\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot ({\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}x+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x) & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}x{\\operatorname{cos}}^{3}x+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x.\n$$"] [17592186335816 "First, we factor ${\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n{\\operatorname{sin}}^{5}x+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x{\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x={\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x\\cdot ({\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}x+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}x+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x\\cdot ({\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}x+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x) & ={\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\operatorname{sin}}^{5}x+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x{\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x={\\operatorname{sin}}^{3}x.\n$$"] [17592186335817 "First, we factor ${\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x$  from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}x{\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x+{\\operatorname{cos}}^{4}x+{\\operatorname{sin}}^{2}x={\\operatorname{cos}}^{2}x\\cdot ({\\operato